DFT-FE 1.2.0 (7147faa51f7c9f3075fffaa5e48ba989bcd329c1) -- qualify two isnan() calls as std::isnan

Class: source compatibility fix (2 lines; no numerics: the calls only detect NaN
in a diagnostic branch of AtomicCenteredNonLocalOperator::compute...).
Problem: src/atom/AtomicCenteredNonLocalOperator.cc lines 785/791 call the
unqualified `isnan(...)` inside a template; C++ provides std::isnan (<cmath>), and
the unqualified spelling only compiles when some header drags in the C macro.
With GCC 14.2.1 and deal.II 9.6.2's headers this fails ("there are no arguments to
'isnan' that depend on a template parameter ... 'isnan' was not declared in this
scope"). Upstream's publicGithubDevelop branch no longer contains these calls.
Fix: `std::isnan`. Conditions: any compiler; applied for this profile. Impact:
none on results. Verified: DFT-FE real builds; results validated in
level3/dftfe/validate.sh. Applied by level3/dftfe/build.sh (git apply,
idempotent); hash recorded in the profile fingerprint.

